Subject: mkksym -k: the block lists the names of the kernel's minor

A kernel cut lists only the names its kabi minor exports (C3-2 version
2 section 2): mkksym -k <tag> skips every list line whose since is
above the tag's minor.  Without -k every name is listed, as before.
The post-link gate reads the same tag from dlm_ident, so a kernel that
claims a minor without its providers fails there.

